response:
The transformation matrix for a reflection over the y-axis is given by \[
    \begin{pmatrix}
      -1 & 0 \\
      0 & 1
    \end{pmatrix}
\]Multiplying this matrix by the vector \[
    \begin{pmatrix}
      -4 \\
      3
    \end{pmatrix}
\] we get \[
    \begin{pmatrix}
      -4 \\
      3
    \end{pmatrix}
\begin{pmatrix}
      -1 & 0 \\
      0 & 1
    \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix}
      4 \\
      3
    \end{pmatrix}
\] Therefore the reflection takes $\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$ to $\boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}}.$</think> <answer> $\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\ 3 \end{pmatrix}$ </answer>

